RF.put("questb:b23",{"8663":{"id":8663,"t":"Doomcaller's Trousers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nSkin of the Great Sandworm Ouro\n2 Idol of Rebirth Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Gold Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Clay Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"You seek to prove your worth to my kind, mortal? Very well, perhaps we can be of mutual assistance.\nThe ancient sandworm, Ouro, is a being of legendary power. He is rumored to have been created by the Old God himself as a mockery of life.\nHis skin is unnatural... thick, nearly impregnable, yet it's flexible and allows him to move with the speed and grace of a much smaller creature.\nBring me a sample of his skin along with other minor components and I shall craft you leggings of great power.","rew":"You will receive:\nDoomcaller's Trousers\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"Yes... the worm's skin will make for an excellent protective layer. Combined with the strongest parts from the Qiraji we've destroyed on our way here, this should make for a formidable piece of armor. May it aid you in facing the unspeakable horrors that await inside!\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warlock Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8663\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Doomcaller's Trousers this quest\nBring the Skin of the Great Sandworm, 2 Idols of Rebirth, 5 Gold Scarabs and 5 Clay Scarabs to Kandrostrasz inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8503":{"id":8503,"t":"The Alliance Needs Stranglekelp!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 37.","obj":"Bring 20 Stranglekelp to Private Draxlegauge at the Military Ward in Ironforge.\n20 Stranglekelp Stranglekelp , Apothecary Quinard 61.5 % , General Kirika 61.5 % , Marshal Bluewall 61.5 % and 4 more","desc":"So, ‹class›, did I already tell you about all of the fabulous uses stranglekelp has? I did? Oh well... in any case we need a lot of it, and when I say a lot, I mean A LOT! Do you think that you could help us out? I know that it means going without all of those wonderful things that you can make with it, but it's for a good cause!","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Alliance Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"It's not true! I'd never skim any stranglekelp off the top of the stacks here. One might be tempted to though considering that it's practically a panacea of utilitarian usefulness. *cough* You don't happen to have that stranglekelp we discussed earlier?","done":"Hooray! That's another twenty down. You're the best. I suppose that I should get these all packed away before they wither. So much stranglekelp, so little time!\nThanks again, ‹class›!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.5,"y":32.7,"n":"Private Draxlegauge","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8583":{"id":8583,"t":"The Horde Needs More Purple Lotus!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Purple Lotus to Apothecary Jezel at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Purple Lotus Elder Torntusk 40 % , Constrictor Vine 1.9 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 1.9 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 1.9 % and 4 more","desc":"In fact it does appear that we are in need of even more purple lotus, ‹class›. While my own studies have yet to determine a new useful application for the herb, there are tried and true methodologies yet to be employed.\nI need you to once again go out into the field and collect at least twenty purple lotus samples. Return them to me here.","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"Excellent and precise work, ‹name›. Your diligence is to be commended, as is your celerity. I will personally see to it that none of these purple lotus go to waste.\nThank you again, and should you come by more purple lotus do not hesitate to bring them to me with utmost haste.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Apothecary Jezel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7223":{"id":7223,"t":"Armor Scraps","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Armor Scraps to Murgot Deepforge in Dun Baldar.\n20 Armor Scraps Winterax Warrior 80 % , Winterax Mystic 80 % , Corporal Teeka Bloodsnarl 80 % , Alliance Sentinel 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Battles rage constantly in Alterac Valley, and the supplies we get from Ironforge are not enough to outfit our experienced troops.\nIf you find armor scraps from the battlefield, aid the war effort and bring those scraps to me!","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Stormpike Guard\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Did you bring any armor scraps, ‹name›?","done":"These are some good pieces, ‹name›. I can use them to fashion new equipment for our troops.\nIf my supply level gets high enough, then maybe our seasoned fighting units will enter the field!\nStart Murgot Deepforge Alterac Valley End Murgot Deepforge Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7223\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Armor Scraps this quest\nBring 20 Armor Scraps to Murgot Deepforge in Dun Baldar.\nMurgot Deepforge Alterac Valley\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] More Armor Scraps\nMurgot Deepforge Alterac Valley","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8263":{"id":8263,"t":"Defiler's Basic Care Package","lv":34,"min":25,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nDefiler's Basic Care Package\nExperience: 270\n+10 reputation with The Defilers","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.4,"y":29.7,"n":"Rutherford Twing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"663":{"id":663,"t":"Land Ho!","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talk to Captain O'Breen in Faldir's Cove.","desc":"Lolo sees a tiny ‹race›! Always on the lookout, Lolo is!\nWelcome to Faldir's Cove. Captain O'Breen said we'd only be here for a few hours. Just long enough to gather the treasure and get back to Booty Bay.\nBut Lolo thinks we're going to be here a lot longer than that. We lost the other two ships from our formation. Poor Spirit of Silverpine and Maiden's Folly. On the bottom of the sea they rest now!\nLolo suggests you talk to Captain O'Breen if you plan on sticking around here.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Booty Bay\n-125 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","done":"Ahoy, matey.\n'Twas a horrible mess. Seahorn will have my ship if he finds out what went down.\nOne of the Professor's contraptions indicated the lost treasure was near this cove. I brought the Harbinger in to dock and signaled for the Spirit of Silverpine and Maiden's Folly to follow suit.\nThen the sea rumbled. The tides lowered and the two ships crashed into the reef.\nIt's not just a reef. Something's down there....\nHelp my crew out and you'll be rewarded handsomely.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":31.8,"y":82.7,"n":"Lolo the Lookout","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.3,"y":81.4,"n":"Shakes O'Breen","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"6503":{"id":6503,"t":"Ashenvale Outrunners","lv":24,"min":19,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 9 Ashenvale Outrunners, then return to Kuray'bin at Splintertree Outpost.\nAshenvale Outrunner slain : 0/ 9","desc":"We received reports that Ashenvale outrunners left Silverwing Outpost not long ago, and now sneak near our territories in the forest. We don't want them gathering intelligence on our defenses!\nSneak through the forests south of our post here and east of the Alliance outpost of Silverwing. Find and slay the outrunners, then return to me.","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"I await reports of your outrunner kills, ‹name›.","done":"Very good, ‹name›. Your hunting skills are impressive...\nThe loss of those outrunners help blind the Alliance, and when they lack intelligence they are less likely to launch attacks.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":71.1,"y":68.1,"n":"Kuray'bin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"23":{"id":23,"t":"Ursangous's Paw","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ursangous's Paw to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\nUrsangous's Paw Ursangous\nProvided: Ursangous's Paw","desc":"<The paw of the mighty bear Ursangous is your trophy for this part of the Ashenvale Hunt. On the paw is a small quarter-crescent emblem; the significance of the emblem remains a mystery.\nThe paw should be brought to Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post to prove that you have bested the mighty creature and completed this portion of the hunt.>","rew":"Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Ah - ‹name› - I was just thinking about you! How goes your hunting?","done":"Ah, the paw of Ursangous! Your skill is impressive, ‹class›; he is credited with numerous kills. The crescent on his paw is no doubt a sign that he was trained by the night elves that skulk about Ashenvale. Ursangous is... was one of the mightiest bears you'd find in these parts. To have bested such a creature is a testament to your will and resolve.\nYour ancestors would be proud!","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"7863":{"id":7863,"t":"Sentinel Basic Care Package","lv":34,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nSentinel Basic Care Package\nExperience: 270\n+10 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Warsong Gulch.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Gulch, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Friendly with us, and bandages when you are Honored.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":61.5,"y":83.9,"n":"Illiyana Moonblaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6823":{"id":6823,"t":"Agent of Hydraxis","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 60.","obj":"Earn an Honored faction with the Hydraxian Waterlords, then talk to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\nReach 9000 reputation with Hydraxian Waterlords","desc":"If you truly wish an allegiance with us, then I invite you to wage war on our foes, the servants of air and earth and fire. Each defeat you heap upon them will weaken their foothold here, and further prove your adherence to our cause.\nThe campaign will be long, but if you persevere then your glory and honor will be great.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","done":"Your exploits against our enemies ring through the chambers of the Waterlords, ‹name›. It was thought by some that your form is too small and fragile to fight in our war, but you have made great gains. You have earned respect among us, an unbelievable feat.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4263":{"id":4263,"t":"Incendius!","lv":56,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Lord Incendius in Blackrock Depths and destroy him!\nLord Incendius slain","desc":"Are you sure Pyron said 'Incendius' when he died?\n<Jalinda swallows hard.>\nLord Incendius is purported to be a minion of Ragnaros! Oh dear, oh dear... whatever will we do?\nDo you think you can handle another mission? I don't have anybody else to send, ‹name›!\nWe will never get a team in if Incendius continues to raise Pyron from the ashes.\nYou'll have to find and destroy Lord Incendius!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSunborne Cape Nightfall Gloves Crypt Demon Bracers Stalwart Clutch\nMoney: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,800\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Is the fiend dead??","done":"Oh dear! Are you sure Incendius said 'Ragnaros?'\n<Jalinda hands you something and pats you on the wrist as she fades deep into thought.>","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":85.4,"y":70.1,"n":"Jalinda Sprig","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4983":{"id":4983,"t":"Bijou's Reconnaissance Report","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take Bijou's Reconnaissance Report back to Grandmaster Lexlort in Kargath.\nBijou's Reconnaissance Report\nProvided: Bijou's Reconnaissance Report","desc":"Take this report back to Lexlort. It will redeem my good name and will surely give the K.E.F. a strategic advantage in dealing with these orcs.\nCome with you? I've got way too much work to do. Get going, they need these reports as soon as possible!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFreewind Gloves Seapost Girdle\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,400\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Where's the goblin???","done":"I've got to hand it to her; she's managed to weasel her way out of another sticky situation! These reports will prove to be invaluable in our dealings with the Blackrock orcs.\nOf course, you will be rewarded for your hard work.","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.9,"y":47.6,"n":"Lexlort","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4743":{"id":4743,"t":"Seal of Ascension","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh. Find the ancient drake, Emberstrife and beat him without mercy until his will is broken.\nIt is at that moment which you must place the Unforged Seal of Ascension before the great beast. You must then be quick to use the Orb of Draconic Energy on his weakened form and claim dominion over his mental faculties. Control the beast and force the Flames of the Black Dragonflight upon the Unforged Seal of Ascension!\nForged Seal of Ascension Forged Seal of Ascension\nProvided: Vaelan's Gift","desc":"Few of the black dragonkin, outside of those in the upper citadel, have the ability to forge the seal with their own flaming breath. Wyrmthalak is one such dragonkin, but his will is unbreakable.\nYou must travel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh. It is there that you will find an ancient drake known as Emberstrife. You must break his will, ‹name›. Break it and use this orb on his weakened form. You will have scant seconds to control his mind and fan the flames that will forge the seal.","rew":"You will receive:\nSeal of Ascension\nExperience: 9,950","back":"Waste no time, ‹name›. Nefarian works feverishly to unleash his evil upon our world.","done":"Stand steady while I cast the final invocation of protection.\n<Vaelan's eyes turn to twin orbs of flame.>\nThe Seal of Ascension is complete...\nKnow this, I have imbued the artifact with some powerful protective wards. In your darkest hour, when all appears to be lost, the might of the red flight will be at your disposal.\nStart Vaelan End Vaelan Level 60 , requires level 57 Difficulty 57 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 4743\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 18,250 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Seal of Ascension\nFind the three gemstones of command: The Gemstone of Smolderthorn, Gemstone of Spirestone, and Gemstone of Bloodaxe.\nVaelan\n8,300 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Seal of Ascension this quest\nTravel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh.\nVaelan\n9,950 XP","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4903":{"id":4903,"t":"Warlord's Command","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 8,550, 0.97 times as much.","obj":"Slay Highlord Omokk, War Master Voone, and Overlord Wyrmthalak. Recover Important Blackrock Documents. Return to Warlord Goretooth in Kargath when the mission has been accomplished.\nImportant Blackrock Documents Bloodaxe Veteran , Smolderthorn Berserker , Spirestone Warlord , Spirestone Ogre Magus and 4 more\nOverlord Wyrmthalak slain\nHighlord Omokk slain\nWar Master Voone slain","desc":"By order of Warlord Goretooth, the following inhabitants of Blackrock Spire must be destroyed:\nThe rotund menace, Highlord Omokk.\nThe cruel and ruthless troll, War Master Voone.\nOverlord Wyrmthalak, taskmaster of the lesser city.\nYou will also be required to return any important documents that you may find.\nSucceed and be honored.\nFail and be forgotten.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWyrmthalak's Shackles Omokk's Girth Restrainer Halycon's Muzzle Vosh'gajin's Strand Voone's Vice Grips\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 8,300\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"<Warlord Goretooth salutes.>","done":"<Warlord Goretooth's dull green skin turns a pasty white for a brief moment.>","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":5.8,"y":47.5,"n":"Warlord Goretooth","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"2583":{"id":2583,"t":"A Boar's Vitality","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Blasted Boar Lungs, two Scorpok Pincers, and one Basilisk Brain to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Blasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %\n2 Scorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %\nBasilisk Brain Redstone Basilisk 40 % , Redstone Crystalhide 40 % , Deatheye 30 %","desc":"Within these blasted lands exists two species of boar: the ash-mane boar and the helboar.\nIt would appear that the stamina of these beasts renders them nearly immune to harm, as the other animals find them too difficult to kill and consequently, not worth the effort.\nWe need to perform further analysis, ‹name›. Should you bring me three blasted boar lungs, two scorpok pincers, and one basilisk brain, I shall create a divine elixir from the residue of the assay. You will be my first test subject!","rew":"You will receive:\nLung Juice Cocktail\nExperience: 4,700","back":"Where are the organs, ‹name›!?","done":"The spirit of the boar illuminates your being, ‹name›! I wonder, do you believe yourself to be as invulnerable as these beasts?","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"2743":{"id":2743,"t":"The Cover of Darkness","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to the Fallen Hero of the Horde with your findings.","desc":"Let us not mince words, ‹race›; my time here is limited.\nYou must destroy the triad of power which protects the demon lord, Razelikh. Doing so will not be as simple a task as freeing a damned soul.\n<Kirith grins.>\nYou see, each of Razelikh's underlings wears a third of an amulet of Razelikh's creation around their neck. The very same amulet you will need in order to summon the arch demon.\nReturn to Trebor and tell him what is required to summon Razelikh. He will be able to instruct you further.","rew":"Experience: 3,300","done":"The demon lord displays a cunning almost as calculated as his brutality, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4023":{"id":4023,"t":"A Taste of Flame","lv":54,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show Cyrus Therepentous proof of your worth.\nYou have a feeling that Cyrus already knows that you are unworthy.\nBlack Dragonflight Molt Frenzied Black Drake 96.4 % , Dark Iron Taskmaster 0 % , Heavy War Golem 0 %","desc":"You seek out the Flight? Present to me proof of your worth, mortal.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"<Cyrus's eyes form two blazing spheres.>","done":"<Cyrus examines the molt.>\nYou have proven that you are not entirely useless, mortal.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":95.1,"y":31.6,"n":"Cyrus Therepentous","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"4183":{"id":4183,"t":"The True Masters","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Lakeshire and deliver Helendis Riverhorn's Letter to Magistrate Solomon.\nHelendis Riverhorn's Letter\nProvided: Helendis Riverhorn's Letter","desc":"We had always assumed that the Blackrock orcs were a product of their savage upbringing. What we have found here, in their homeland, tells us another story.\nIndeed, it is bloodlust and thirst for conflict that empowers them, but the black dragonflight are the beings whom control the orcs of Blackrock. We suspect that it is the black dragonflight that fuels them with rage and hostility.\nTake this letter to Magistrate Solomon. He will know what must be done.\n<Helendis hands you a sealed letter.>","rew":"Experience: 4,100\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Greetings, ‹name›. Have we met before? You look vaguely familiar.","done":"<Magistrate Solomon opens the sealed letter from Helendis and begins reading.>\nBurning Steppes Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":85.8,"y":68.9,"n":"Helendis Riverhorn","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97943":{"id":97943,"t":"Camping 101 fishing","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Astaia in Darnassus to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your fishing skill to 20","desc":"You might not think so, but your skill as a fisherman can actually come in handy at camp.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Fish Bowl for your camp. You can use this fixture to help provide a bit of joy to yourself and your fellow adventurers. A happy adventurer is a strong adventurer and I'm sure your combat capabilities will reflect that.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Fish Bowl. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":47.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Astaia","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94263":{"id":94263,"t":"Craftsmans writ fire protection potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Fire Protection Potion\nFire Protection Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Fire Protection Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Fire Protection Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94263","cats":["crafting"]},"94343":{"id":94343,"t":"Craftsmans writ wicked leather pants","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Wicked Leather Pants\nWicked Leather Pants","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Wicked Leather Pants, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Wicked Leather Pants Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94343","cats":["crafting"]},"7943":{"id":7943,"t":"More Bat Eyes","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Evil Bat Eye Bloodseeker Bat 40.9 % in Zul'Gurub , Duskwing 28.8 % , Monstrous Plaguebat 28.4 % , Plaguebat 27.6 % and 3 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","back":"‹name›, the attraction I'm designing will be the scariest event since Gnomeregan was overrun! And it's largely thanks to you and all the baubles you've brought me. Many, many thanks!\nI don't need much else, but... if you bring me more evil bat eyes from the bats of the Eastern Plaguelands... I might have more Darkmoon Faire tickets for you.","done":"Thanks again, ‹name›. Here are your tickets!\nElwynn Forest Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.2,"y":69.5,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Yebb Neblegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"983":{"id":983,"t":"Buzzbox 827","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 6 Crawler Legs and place them in Buzzbox 827.\n6 Crawler Leg Raging Reef Crawler , Pygmy Tide Crawler 80 % , Tide Crawler 80 % , Encrusted Tide Crawler 80 % and 2 more","desc":"Hey! Help me with my latest invention, the buzzbox. You can talk to people far away!\nMaybe you've already seen them, they're boxes with levers on them. The only problem is they need constant maintenance.\nEach one suffers from a different problem, but I made a really smart decision. I placed each one near creatures that have the proper parts to fix that particular machine. Right now Buzzbox 827 is on the fritz. It's just south of Auberdine, real close. It takes 6 Crawler Legs to fix it. I'll pay ya...","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"Buzzbox 827 sits with an eerie silence. A single flashing light indicates that it needs 6 Crawler Legs to be placed in its holding box.","done":"As you place the Crawler Legs inside the machine, you hear gears begin to grind. Judging from the banging sounds coming from the Buzzbox, you believe the Crawler Legs are being put in their proper place. Soon the machine begins to hum, and you hear a tiny voice calling out from within.\n\"Hello? Uhh... Hello! You fixed it! This is Wizbang by the way! Thanks a lot... Hey, you wouldn't want to fix another one, would ya?\"","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37,"y":44.1,"n":"Wizbang Cranktoggle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":46.3,"n":"Buzzbox 827","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6343":{"id":6343,"t":"Return to Nessa","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Laird's Response to Nessa Shadowsong.\nLaird's Response\nProvided: Laird's Response","desc":"I must send a response to Nessa. She'll be very interested to know how different the fish here are from those along Teldrassil's coastline. We can only guess the cause, but it is my suspicion that the world tree itself is affecting the wildlife around it!\nPlease, take this response to Nessa. If you wish to take a hippogryph back to Rut'theran then speak with the hippogryph master Caylais Moonfeather. If you wish to take the ferry, then one regularly departs from the dock to the northwest.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"‹name›, you're back from Auberdine? Did you speak with Laird?","done":"This is very interesting. The fish here are large, but I didn't think the difference in bounties between here and the mainland was so great. There must be a reason for this...\nWell thank you, ‹name›. I will discuss with the villagers the news you brought. Perhaps, one day, we will find the root of this oddity. But until then, we shall reap its benefits!\nDarkshore Teldrassil","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.8,"y":44.3,"n":"Laird","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.3,"y":92.4,"n":"Nessa Shadowsong","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1143":{"id":1143,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":31,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,500 experience instead of 2,450, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Kill Athrikus Narassin and bring his head to Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx.\nAthrikus Narassin's Head Athrikus Narassin","desc":"I see. Well, if what you say is true, then now is the time to strike. I believe Athrikus resides at the top of the tower. Be careful though, he is surrounded by many powerful warlocks, much more deadly than the ones you faced before.","rew":"Experience: 2,500\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Athrikus Narassin is an ancient and powerful warlock. Perhaps we should wait for Delgren's assistance, but he obviously had much faith in you to send you alone.","done":"With the death of Athrikus, I hope that the demonic forces in this area will be driven back. I have no doubt that they will regroup and return, but then we shall be even more prepared to meet their threat.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"98903":{"id":98903,"t":"The battle for darkspear islands","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Win a Darkspear Islands battleground and return back to Brelinda McFarry at Northwatch Hold.\nWin in Darkspear Islands","desc":"Go forth and represent the Theramore Expeditionary Force in battle at Darkspear Islands, ‹name›! Achieve victory and show these Horde dogs the might of the Alliance!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,000\n+200 reputation with Theramore Expeditionary Force","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63.4,"y":58.6,"n":"Brelinda McFarry","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkspear-islands"]},"5943":{"id":5943,"t":"Gizelton Caravan","lv":38,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Farseer's Forgotten Shield.","obj":"Escort the Gizelton Caravan through Mannoroc Coven. Talk with Smeed at Scrabblescrew's Camp for your reward.","desc":"You look like a capable ‹race›. Perhaps you're looking to make some money? Cork and I started this caravan to make a bundle of money; little did we know the dangers of turning a buck!\nUp ahead is Mannoroc Coven... normally the demons ignore us but something has the kodos spooked this time. I'll pay you to protect the caravan past Mannoroc Coven. Once we are safely past you can receive your reward from our business associate Smeed at Scrabblescrew's Camp.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSidegunner Shottie Kodo Brander Studded Ring Shield Farseer's Forgotten Shield\nNew in Forever: Farseer's Forgotten Shield.\nExperience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"You know, if that caravan were to ever disappear I would be ruined! You're not the bearer of bad news about the caravan, are you?\n<Smeed wipes his brow.>\nThank the goddess of greed!","done":"Not sure it's a prosperous proposition to be paying so much money to protect the Gizelton Caravan. Cork and Rigger only make one gold piece a week, but as long as they keep paying for my kodos I can care less how they run their business.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":60.3,"y":38.2,"n":"Rigger Gizelton","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":60.9,"y":61.9,"n":"Smeed Scrabblescrew","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"92743":{"id":92743,"t":"A conquerors crown","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\nConqueror's Helm\nMagram Clan Centaur","desc":"As the strongest centaur clan in all the land, we deserve armaments with ferocity that matches our strength!\nWarug needs one most of all. A helm... no, a crown! A conqueror's crown! I heard legends of a fearsome conqueror across the seas. Go to a place they call the Badlands and seek out a crypt there. Return to me only when you have found the crown.\nDo this for me, and I will reveal the Magram's greatest strength.\nLevel 40 , requires level 30 Difficulty 30 36 38 43 51 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 92743\nThe chain\n15 quests from level 32 to 43, 36,630 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Brutal Politics\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Assault on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram.\nWarug Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Magram Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Magram, then speak with Warug.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 33 ] Broken Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Broken Tears to Warug in the Magram Village.\nWarug Desolace\n2,650 XP\n4 [ 40 ] A Conqueror's Crown this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and return a Conqueror's Crown from the Badlands to Warug in Magram Village.\n3,150 XP\n5 [ 40 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Magram, and locate Orgrul near the Valley of Bones south of Magram Village.\n320 XP\n6 [ 42 ] Mountain of Bones\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 426 Gently Cursed Bones to Orgrul south of the Magram Village in Desolace.\n3,450 XP\n7 [ 42 ] Corrupting Tears\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram, and bring 3 Petrified Bark and 3 Imbued Tears back to Orgrul.\n3,450 XP\n8 [ 41 ] Proof of Concept\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, then bring 426 Well Cursed Bones from a successful ritual back to Orgrul.\n2,450 XP\n9 [ 40 ] Bone Raising\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and use the Enhanced Necromancy Staff to fully raise undead that are struggling to emerge throughout the Valley of Bones.\n2,350 XP\n[ 42 ] No Mercy for the Weak\nMaintain your reputation with the Magram Clan, and slay 5 Gelkis Captives scattered around the Valley of Bones.\n2,550 XP\n10 [ 43 ] B","cats":["desolace"]},"7463":{"id":7463,"t":"Arcane Refreshment","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the Warpwood Quarter of Dire Maul and slay the water elemental, Hydrospawn. Return to Lorekeeper Lydros in the Athenaeum with the Hydrospawn Essence.\nHydrospawn Essence Hydrospawn","desc":"A ‹race› mage! How wonderous. I have not seen one of your kind for... oh what is it going on now? 500 years!\nI have something that will quench your thirst, but first you must do a task for me.\n<Lydros snickers.>\nThere is an anomaly in Eldre'Thalas. A water elemental has taken residence in the east wing. His presence must be catalogued!\nVenture to the Warpwood Quarter and extract a portion of the elemental essence of the Hydrospawn. Return it to me and I shall teach you a useful cantrip.","rew":"You will learn: Conjure Water\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"Yes? Do I know you?","done":"Wonderful! Who are you again? Oh it matters not. What was I supposed to give you? Hrm... well you are a ‹class›, perhaps you will find this useful.\nAlterac Mountains Open the zone on the world map Start Lorekeeper Lydros End Lorekeeper Lydros Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Mage Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 7463","cats":["dire-maul"]},"7703":{"id":7703,"t":"Unfinished Gordok Business","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Gauntlet of Gordok Might and return it to Captain Kromcrush in Dire Maul.\nAccording to Kromcrush, the \"old timey story\" says that Tortheldrin - a \"creepy\" elf who called himself a prince - stole it from one of the Gordok kings.\nGauntlet of Gordok Might The Prince's Chest","desc":"Now you da king, so maybe you get prized Gordok artifact back from creepy elf who calls himself Prince! Da king before you failed, just like all da other kings since Tortheldrin - da creepy elf - stole it from old timey Gordok king!\nArtifact is called da Gauntlet of Gordok Might. Old timey stories say only da one true king da Gordok can get it back. Old timey story also say creepy elf is still around here - you find it and it will become mighty gauntlet you wear forever! Yar, I show you!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGordok's Handguards Gordok's Gauntlets Gordok's Gloves Gordok's Handwraps\nExperience: 8,300","back":"Hah, you no find it, do you boss? Maybe old timey story a bad story... hard to believe that creepy elf can steal from Gordok king!","done":"Wow... you ARE da true king/queen! I never think I see this gauntlet in my life! It look like it got no mojo left anymore... maybe that creepy elf try and ruin gauntlet. Well, I say HAR HAR to him!\nLook - this mark on da gauntlet an old old OLD timey magic mark, older than da Gordok they say. Well, as Captain of da Gordok, we all learn one thing over and over - how to make mark come to life and give power back to gauntlet!\nI do it for you, king/queen! Here, take da gauntlet and rule FOREVER!\nSilverpine Forest Open the zone on the world map Start Captain Kromcrush End Captain Kromcrush Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7703","cats":["dire-maul"]},"9063":{"id":9063,"t":"Torwa Pathfinder","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Torwa Pathfinder in Un'Goro Crater.","desc":"A hunter by the name of Torwa Pathfinder has requested the help of a druid. He said only we would possess the necessary skills and respect for nature to help him.\nThere is a road that connects the Un'Goro Crater and the desert of Tanaris. As that road enters the crater, you will find Torwa close by.","rew":"Experience: 500","done":"You have traveled far to meet with me, ‹class›, and not a moment too soon.\nThunder Bluff Darnassus Stormwind City Feralas Felwood Moonglade Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":76.5,"y":27.2,"n":"Turak Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":77.1,"y":27,"n":"Sheal Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":7.4,"n":"Denatharion","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":35.8,"y":67.4,"n":"Sheldras Moontree","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":36.1,"y":64.4,"n":"Theridran","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":76,"y":42.3,"n":"Jannos Lighthoof","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":61.9,"y":24.5,"n":"Golhine the Hooded","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":52.5,"y":40.6,"n":"Loganaar","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":71.6,"y":76,"n":"Torwa Pathfinder","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"183":{"id":183,"t":"The Boar Hunter","lv":3,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talin Keeneye would like you to kill 12 Small Crag Boars.\nSmall Crag Boar slain : 0/ 12","desc":"Nothing like a day of boar hunting, eh?\nThough, here in Coldridge Valley, there are so many boars it almost takes the fun out of it. No need to get them charging. They're all angry and ready without any help. In fact, recently, there've been so many boars in the area, it's become dangerous for me to do my daily hunting.\nLong story short, if you could help me kill some of the boars, I would appreciate it.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDwarven Cloth Britches Dwarven Leather Pants\nExperience: 250\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"How goes the hunt?","done":"Excellent! I can go back to my... leisurely... hunting now. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":22.6,"y":71.4,"n":"Talin Keeneye","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"98423":{"id":98423,"t":"The Treaty of Understanding","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Deliver the Treaty of Understanding to Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.\nProvided: Treaty of Understanding","desc":"Inside of the vault you find a tablet detailing the terms of a peace treaty between the Bronzebeard and Wildhammer dwarf clans. It appears to date back to time period just after of the War of the Three Hammers, and is very likely a notable piece of dwarven history. The king of Ironforge would no doubt be interested in this artifact.","rew":"Money: 16 0 gold, 16 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"What have you brought from the depths, ‹class›.","done":"Ah yes, my ancestor Madoran was the first Bronzebeard king of Ironforge following the great civil war between the Wildhammer, Bronzebeard, and Dark Iron clans. This treaty was drafted to codify the cessation of hostilities and terms of peace after the Bronzebeards won the mountain.\nAs you can see, the Wildhammers and Bronzebeards signed it... and the Dark Irons did not.\nThank you for recovering this and bringing it to me, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Ironforge","x":39.4,"y":55.8,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"823":{"id":823,"t":"Report to Orgnil","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.","desc":"We at Sen'jin Village are not without our own troubles, and we thank you for your aid. But the news you bring regarding the Burning Blade could be trouble for everyone.\nThere is an orc stationed at Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar, who polices Durotar from evils such as the Burning Blade! Go to Orgnil and tell him of our plight, as well as your news from the Valley of Trials. He will want to know these things.\nRazor Hill lies to the north.","rew":"Experience: 320\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Yes? You have something to report? Well then, let's have it!","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":52.2,"y":43.2,"n":"Orgnil Soulscar","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"97223":{"id":97223,"t":"Bloodtalon matriarch","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Eggs of the Bloodtalon Matriarch to Xar'Ti in Sen'jin Village.\nBloodtalon Matriarch Eggs","desc":"All of the raptors you see before you are ones I have trained myself. They come from all over Kalimdor, but some of the finest come from the Bloodtalon raptors on the isles off our coast.\nOne raptor amongst them, the Bloodtalon Matriarch, is particularly savage and has killed many from our village and has become too dangerous to leave at our borders. If you can strike her down, return with her eggs so that we can raise the hatchlings as allies instead of enemies.","rew":"You will receive:\nRaptorscale Pants\nMoney: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The Bloodtalon are known for their cunning and swiftness, and make fine companions when raised from egg to adult.\nUnfortunately adult raptors are very difficult to train, and I have tried to capture the Matriarch on more than one occasion. But she had become too dangerous of late.\nStill I hope to preserve her legacy by raising her children as companions here in Sen'Jin.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I am happy we will be able to preserve her bloodline and raise them to be our allies. You have done a great service for our tribe.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":55.2,"y":75.4,"n":"Xar'Ti","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"1383":{"id":1383,"t":"Nothing But The Truth","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Apothecary Faustin at Beggar's Haunt needs 5 Shadow Panther Hearts, Mire Lord Fungus and a Deep Strider Tumor.\n5 Shadow Panther Heart Shadow Panther 35 %\nMire Lord Fungus Mire Lord\nDeepstrider Tumor Deepstrider Searcher , Deepstrider Giant","desc":"I have just the right serum in mind. It will deal with the truth in precisely the way the truth should be dealt with.\nFor this concoction I will need several Shadow Panther hearts from the Swamp. I also require the enchanted fungus off of the Mire Lord who resides there. I am sure one as able as you, ‹name›, can persuade him to part with some.\nNow the hard part will be locating a Deepstrider tumor from far-off Desolace. Very rarely the giants there become ill and a tumor forms.\nNow, off you go!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCloak of Blight Cragwood Maul\nExperience: 4,300\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"That Infiltrator in Stonard will surely.... open up... after he drinks my special serum. Haha!\nThe ingredients required are by no means easy to procure. Shadow Panthers are common in the Swamp but collecting enough hearts for our purpose can be daunting. And the Mire Lord can be such a fussy beast.\nAs for the Deepstrider tumor, they are terribly difficult to find. But the chemical reaction I can draw from it is second to none.","done":"Splendid, ‹name›! And just in time too. From what Zraedus tells me, the Infiltrator has recovered from his wounds and is ready to be questioned by the orcs.\nGive me but a moment to prepare the pois - I mean prepare the truth serum.\nDuskwood Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":87.5,"y":35.2,"n":"Apothecary Faustin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"6583":{"id":6583,"t":"The Test of Skulls, Somnus","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,250, 0.91 times as much.","obj":"Destroy the drake champion of the Green Flight, Somnus. Take his skull and return it to Emberstrife.\nThe Skull of Somnus Somnus","desc":"Just as our Father crushes the Aspects themselves, so too must we strive to bring chaos and destruction to their children.\nYou must test your battle prowess against the sleepless dreamers: The children of the Green Flight.\nTravel to the Swamp of Sorrows and track down Somnus, drake champion of the Green Flight. Let flow your hatred; dominate the insect... Return to me with his skull...","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Do not return here until you have bathed in the blood of our enemies and drank in their suffering.","done":"Another complete...\nDustwallow Marsh Swamp of Sorrows","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5543":{"id":5543,"t":"Blood Tinged Skies","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Plaguebats and return to Tirion Fordring.\nPlaguebat slain : 0/ 30","desc":"Woe to those that foolishly wander into the Plaguelands. All manner of foulness inhabit these woods - from the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, who will kill any that do not bear the mark of the Crusade, to the murderous Scourge, who only look to bolster their numbers by adding more undead to their ranks.\nEven the wildlife have been transformed into rapacious, man eating beasts. I ask that you destroy those that would strike from the skies: The Plaguebats.","rew":"Experience: 5,800","back":"Do not underestimate the winged vermin, ‹race›. The Plague has given them supernatural abilities.","done":"You are a shining example of decency, ‹race›! It has been long since I have felt the blood of heroes pump through my veins. Your acts of bravery are uplifting!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9223":{"id":9223,"t":"Superior Armaments of Battle - Honored Amongst the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 20 Insignias of the Dawn and 20 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n20 Insignia of the Dawn\n20 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of power?\nI must warn you; purchases made at honored reputation with the Dawn come with a fairly prohibitive surcharge. I would advise that you gain a better reputation with the Dawn before moving forward with your plans.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of Piety Band of Resolution Verimonde's Last Resort Supply Bag Leggings of the Plague Hunter Sanctified Leather Helm\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"99143":{"id":99143,"t":"Bottles and baubles","lv":7,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 6 pieces of shiny junk from the nearby Murloc camp.\n6 Shiny Junk","desc":"Those fish men must think like actual fish, right? Which means anything they like, fish will like!\nIf you rummage through some of their junk and return to me with anything that seems like it would make good bait, I'll reward you.","rew":"You will receive:\nShiny Silver Coin\nExperience: 625","back":"What did you find? Anything interesting?","done":"An interesting collection. These should work well enough!\nHere's some of my own older supplies. It should help anyone trying to get their footing in fishing.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":47.4,"y":62.2,"n":"Lee Brown","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"98823":{"id":98823,"t":"Earthen echo","lv":31,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring the Titan Relic to Muln Earthfury at the Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore.\nTitan Relic","desc":"Truly, this is a fascinating object.\nIt shows indications of being much more than a mere carving or sculpture.\nWhile our elders may be interested in observing this artifact, the Earthen Ring are who would carry the most wisdom for our buried ruins and forgotten lands. Seek out Muln Earthfury, a direct approach is fitting for the gravity of what you carry.\nYou can find him and other elders of the Earthen Ring council at the Skywatcher Plateau in northwest Mulgore.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHeavehammer Healer's Staff Furs of the Earthen Ring\nMoney: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,950\nThunder Bluff Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":70.8,"y":33.8,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":33.4,"y":22.4,"n":"Muln Earthfury","e":1}],"cats":["excavation-site-wetlands-dungeon"]},"4343":{"id":4343,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":38.8,"y":21.9,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"4103":{"id":4103,"t":"Salve via Hunting","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Corrupted Soul Shard Ulathek 35 % , Xavaric 35 % , Prince Xavalis 35 % , Jaedenar Legionnaire 35 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Cenarion Plant Salve\nExperience: 4,200","back":"Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to see a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.\nIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.","done":"Very well then, here are your Cenarion plant salves. Scour Felwood for corrupted plants, ‹name›! Wherever they are, use the salve I have given you to purify them.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":54.1,"y":86.8,"n":"Arathandris Silversky","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2903":{"id":2903,"t":"The Battle Plans","lv":43,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Woodpaw Battle Plans to Hadoken Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\nWoodpaw Battle Plans\nProvided: Woodpaw Battle Plans","desc":"With the battle plans of the gnolls discovered, all that now remains is to bring the plans back to Hadoken Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache. Perhaps he or someone there can make further sense of what the gnolls are up to.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEarthclasp Barrier Rushridge Boots\nExperience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Welcome back ‹name› - were you able to find some tangible evidence as to the plans of the gnolls?","done":"Ah, this is exactly what we needed. While I am not so skilled at ciphering what most of the scrawling on this map is, I've seen enough battle plans in my day to understand what is happening with the gnolls. It looks like they are currently fighting a two front war. One is with us... but it seems that their main energy has been against a foe to their south.\nThere's more at hand here than meets the eye. Perhaps it is time to figure out who this other foe they face really is.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":71.6,"y":55.9,"n":"Woodpaw Battle Map","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3063":{"id":3063,"t":"Vengeance on the Northspring","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talo Thornhoof wants you to kill 4 Northspring Harpies, 4 Northspring Roguefeathers, 4 Northspring Windcallers, and 4 Northspring Slayers.\nNorthspring Harpy slain : 0/ 4\nNorthspring Roguefeather slain : 0/ 4\nNorthspring Slayer slain : 0/ 4\nNorthspring Windcaller slain : 0/ 4","desc":"In my day, I was a seasoned hunter. There wasn't any creature around that I feared. Until...\nI was out in the forest, sharpening my blade after a tough battle, when I was ambushed. Harpies surrounded me, and I barely managed to drag myself to safety.\nEven now, I can still hear their cries echoing...\nI was never the same after that. But the hate boils inside of me -- I must get even, after all these years.\nThe Northspring harpies can be found to the west of here. ‹name›, get my revenge.","rew":"Money: 55 0 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,550\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The wings of the Northspring harpies are black as the night; do not take your eyes off of them, lest they disappear into darkness.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You have put an old tauren's mind at peace.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Talo Thornhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"503":{"id":503,"t":"Gol'dir","lv":36,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free Gol'dir then return to Krusk in Tarren Mill.\nRusted Iron Key Jailor Borhuin","desc":"From what I can tell of the documents you procured, Gol'dir is being held in a large Syndicate base to the north, most likely in the Alterac Mountains. He has been held captive far too long and must be freed.","rew":"Experience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Give me the key, ‹class›, I will undo the lock myself.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I led the expedition from Durotar under the Warchief's orders, but as you can see, our plans went somewhat awry. They have held me captive here in this town, forcing me to work, hauling burdens, digging...\nWhat I have suffered is unimportant, however. There is important information you must deliver to whomever is leading our group now.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":60,"y":43.7,"n":"Gol'dir","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6103":{"id":6103,"t":"Training the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Jocaste in the Cenarion Enclave, in Darnassus.","desc":"You now have the power to tame a pet, but you must also gain the skills to train it.\nTravel to Darnassus. There you must speak to one of our most revered hunters, Jocaste. She will give you the ability to train your new pet, so make haste.\nWhile Jocaste may seem stern, she is always pleased to see another hunter rising through the ranks. Treat her with respect and she will return in kind. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"You will learn: Training Lesson\nExperience: 420","done":"A fledgling ‹class›. I see. Yes. I can bestow you with the skills you need to train and guide your pet. Not only will you be able to teach your pet new abilities, you will now be able to feed your pet, as well as revive it, should it fall in battle.\nRemember, ‹name›, always respect the balance and live in awe of nature around you. Now, go forth. We shall speak again, at a later date.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":40.4,"y":8.5,"n":"Jocaste","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"5143":{"id":5143,"t":"Tribal Leatherworking","lv":55,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Wild Leather Vest and a Wild Leather Helmet to Caryssia Moonhunter in Feralas.\nCompleting this quest will give you access to the Tribal Leatherworking arts.\nThe completion of this quest will prevent you from learning Dragonscale Leatherworking and Elemental Leatherworking; be sure this is the path you wish to follow before doing so.\nWild Leather Vest\nWild Leather Helmet","desc":"To learn tribal leatherworking demands an understanding of how primal nature truly is; I know that you have already mastered the art of making wild leather armor, and I am willing to complete your training.\nKnow this, ‹class›: by choosing this path you agree never to learn dragonscale or elemental leatherworking; there is only room for practice of one of the three arts. Furthermore, bring to me the finest samples of your wild leather armor. From there, we will begin your mastery.","rew":"You will learn: Tribal Leatherworking\nExperience: 4,200\n+200 reputation with Leatherworking - Tribal","back":"Nature is a force that must be appeased before you hope to learn how to bend its will into your leather garments. Bring me your offering to this force, and I will make sure you are heard.","done":"You've given your finest offerings, and nature will soon permit you to bend her to your will. Once I have finished my tutelage, your work will be a force of nature unto itself.\nTo train in the art for the future, simply speak to me and I will make available any knowledge that you have yet to commit as yours.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":89.4,"y":46.6,"n":"Caryssia Moonhunter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"263":{"id":263,"t":"In Defense of the King's Lands","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mountaineer Wallbang in the southern guard tower wants you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers.\nStonesplinter Shaman slain : 0/ 10\nStonesplinter Bonesnapper slain : 0/ 10","desc":"The Mountaineers tell me you are quite brave and capable, ‹name›. We need a ‹race› like you around here. The Trogg problem isn't getting any better. The reserves have been called to the front and we're all alone out here. But now that we have a seasoned ‹class› here, let's see what you can do.\nGo out and kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers. Let's see if you live up to your reputation, Trogg-Slayer.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Coarse Sharpening Stone\nMoney: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Back so soon? In case I didn't make myself clear we need you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers, ‹name›. Now go get 'em, Trogg-Slayer!","done":"I knew the second I laid eyes on you, ‹name›, that you would make Ironforge proud. You have served King Magni well. Now that you've proven yourself to be such a loyal aid to the Kingdom, perhaps you should talk with the Captain to see if he'll entrust you with a higher detail.\nI salute you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":23.5,"y":74.5,"n":"Mountaineer Wallbang","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"98983":{"id":98983,"t":"Frostleaf the elder","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance\nLevel 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 98983","cats":["lunar-festival"]},"1943":{"id":1943,"t":"Speak with Deino","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Deino.","desc":"The troll mage Deino has need of your assistance, ‹name›. She resides in Orgrimmar, in the Darkbriar Lodge.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Good, you have come. My task is not an easy one, but vital to the society of mages. If you aid me, I am sure you will find it worthwhile.\nUndercity Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":85.1,"y":10,"n":"Anastasia Hartwell","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":38.4,"y":86.1,"n":"Deino","e":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"743":{"id":743,"t":"Dangers of the Windfury","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Windfury Talons to Ruul Eagletalon in Bloodhoof Village.\n8 Windfury Talon Windfury Wind Witch 80 % , Windfury Harpy 80 %","desc":"Thank you for taking the time to speak to me, ‹name›. I am Ruul, warrior and teacher.\nYou have obviously reached an age when you must prepare for your trials if you are to adventure much further out of Mulgore.\nIf you wish a test of your strength, start by seeking out the Windfury harpies to the southeast. They nestle along the mountain's edges away from the road.\nThey are one of our natural enemies here in Mulgore and will be a good gauge of your skill.","rew":"Money: 2 25 0 gold, 2 silver, 25 copper Experience: 700\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The Windfuries are deadly foes. Their strength in battle is only rivaled by their desire for fresh meat.","done":"You have done well, ‹name›. You seem well prepared to travel onward. Let the wind always be at your back.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.5,"y":64.9,"n":"Ruul Eagletalon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"7783":{"id":7783,"t":"The Lord of Blackrock","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Head of Nefarian to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nHead of Nefarian Nefarian\nProvided: Head of Nefarian","desc":"The old feeling returns. The welcome pangs of victory reverberate throughout your being. Before you lies the monolithic, battle scarred head of Nefarian. Return it to your Warchief, champion.","rew":"Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+200 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+200 reputation with Thunder Bluff\n+200 reputation with Undercity","back":"I wish that I could have been there to see the look on the face of the beast as you struck the killing blow, ‹name›.","done":"You have honored the Horde once more, ‹name›. The son of Deathwing lays dead. Surely, the evil one stirs.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1783":{"id":1783,"t":"The Tome of Divinity","lv":13,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Symbol of Life and resurrect Narm Faulk in Dun Morogh.\nNarm Faulk","desc":"We was spyin' on some of the Dark Iron dwarves that've bunkered down south of Helm's Bed Lake. We knew they was up to no good, so Narm an' me thought we'd take a closer look--got ta see their leader given orders to some o' his men.\nNarm an' me took the chance to kill a few of 'em, but they proved tougher than we thought, an' more of 'em got the jump on us. Narm tol' me to run an' get support, so 'ere I am.\nNarm needs help, an' I'll not rest till he gets it.\nC'n ya help, ‹name›?","rew":"Experience: 675","done":"I can't thank you enough, brother/sister.\nI can only assume that Tiza and Muiredon sent you here to aid me if you carry the Symbol of Life.\nIt's true, I fell to the Dark Iron while trying to attain one of the scripts: I was able to hold on long enough to allow Muiredon to escape, but the Light had almost embraced me fully when you came along. The fact that you were powerful enough to use the Symbol means great things for you, but there's time to speak of that later.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":54.9,"y":22.4,"n":"Muiredon Battleforge","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":78.3,"y":58.1,"n":"Narm Faulk","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5623":{"id":5623,"t":"In Favor of the Light","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Priestess Josetta in Elwynn Forest.","desc":"Hello again, young priest/priestess. The time has come for you to learn more about our religion. After you've completed whatever tasks you have here in Northshire, please seek out Priestess Josetta in Goldshire. She has more to teach you and has heard that you are growing strong in the ways of the Light. She looks forward to tutoring you more.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"I'm glad you've arrived, ‹name›. We have much to discuss about your future and your path within the Light.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Priestess Anetta","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.3,"y":65.7,"n":"Priestess Josetta","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94823":{"id":94823,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"Elune bless you, good ‹race›. I hope your Light finds you and protects you well this day.\nOne of your priests was here not long ago looking for you. He mentioned you returning to the Hall of Mysteries as soon as possible to speak with High Priestess Mims. It seems you've done well to garner such attention. I wouldn't spend too much time here--your people have need of you.\nLevel 10 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 13 16 Side Alliance Class Priest Shareable Yes Quest ID 94823","cats":["priest"]},"8823":{"id":8823,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Horde Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with Orgrimmar. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":30.8,"y":73.7,"n":"Orgrimmar Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":42.5,"y":38.7,"n":"Officer Redblade","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"3463":{"id":3463,"t":"Set Them Ablaze!","lv":52,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Set the North, South, East, and West Sentry Towers on fire by using the Torch of Retribution inside each of the buildings.\nWestern Tower Ablaze\nSouthern Tower Ablaze\nEastern Tower Ablaze\nNorthern Tower Ablaze\nProvided: Torch of Retribution","desc":"Listen well, ‹name›. While the four towers can never be destroyed, you can use the torch of retribution to set them ablaze for a very long period of time: A fire that no element or force can subdue.\nWhile they are ablaze, no guard or sentry unit can inhabit the watch posts and thus, their first line of defense is nullified.\nYou must enter each tower and use the Torch of Retribution within their fortifications. Beware the lookouts posted by the Dark Irons, ‹name›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDragonflight Leggings Drakefire Headguard Axe of the Ebon Drake\nMoney: 2 30 2 gold, 30 silver, 0 copper Experience: 7,600","back":"Are you lost, ‹name›?","done":"It is glorious! Is it not glorious master?","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.2,"y":39,"n":"Squire Maltrake","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8903":{"id":8903,"t":"Dangerous Love","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get a Stormwind Guard's Card and return it to Aristan Mottar in Stormwind.\nStormwind Guard's Card","desc":"There's something unnatural about this epidemic of love. It's not proper, it's an eyesore, and at worst, it could be a threat to the the safety of the Alliance itself.\nJust think: what if the guards have been taken in by this strange affliction? Something must be done.\nGo to one of the guards here in Stormwind and see if they've been caught up in this foolishness.","back":"Was I right to worry? Are the guards afflicted with this lovesickness?","done":"So it is true. This is unbelievable. How could this have happened? Let me think for a moment. There must be a reason behind this.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":75,"n":"Aristan Mottar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7063":{"id":7063,"t":"The Feast of Winter Veil","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Feel free to read the book, \"The Feast of Winter Veil\", to learn more about the holiday. When you are finished with the book, deliver it to King Magni Bronzebeard in Ironforge.\nThe Feast of Winter Veil\nProvided: The Feast of Winter Veil","desc":"Here - if you are interested in learning more about the Feast of Winter Veil, read this book. While I think our recognition of the legend is the appropriate one, I'm enough of a scholar to appreciate the collection of all information into a single source.\nWhen you're done, take the book to King Magni Bronzebeard. I know for a fact he'd be interested in hearing that others have taken an interest in the older legends.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+200 reputation with Ironforge","back":"I bid you welcome to the Kingdom of Ironforge, friend. I always take an interest in those who choose to take an interest in the kingdom, its people, and its lore. Is this why you are standing before me?","done":"The legends and lore surrounding the Winter Veil are ones that have faded from the forefront of public thought over the years. While I recognize that the goblins are helping to revive the season for their own ends, the fact that the citizenry thinks about it at least in some form does good to keep such lore alive.\nYour desire to go beyond the material and learn about our past is an admirable trait, young ‹class›. I salute your erudite nature.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.4,"y":30.1,"n":"King Magni Bronzebeard","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8983":{"id":8983,"t":"Tracing the Source","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mara Rennick at the tailor's shop in the Undercity's Mage Quarter.","desc":"Something's wrong with my product? Well, I've never seen so many people wanting something so badly.\nI bought my supply from a merchant named Mara Rennick. She's new in town.\nShe mentioned she had some goods she had to deliver to the tailor in the Mage Quarter.","done":"I'm afraid I sold my entire supply of perfume and cologne to Norman, the innkeeper. If you'd like some, you should speak with him - assuming he has any left.\nYou shouldn't waste any time, though. I think you'll find the cologne irresistible.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":67.7,"y":37.9,"n":"Innkeeper Norman","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":71.3,"y":28.3,"n":"Mara Rennick","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"6983":{"id":6983,"t":"You're a Mean One...","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 35.","obj":"Locate and return the Stolen Treats to Kaymard Copperpinch in Orgrimmar. It was last thought to be in the possession of the Abominable Greench, found somewhere in the snowy regions of the Alterac Mountains.\nStolen Treats The Abominable Greench","desc":"A c-c-creature called \"The Abominable Greench\" is the one w-w-who stole our shipment of t-t-treats, ‹name›. Be c-c-careful though! He is t-t-the one who turned me into this s-s-snowy mess!\nYou're g-g-gonna need some help in f-f-facing him. I've seen him w-w-wander all around where the y-y-yeti are; he's s-s-surely here s-s-somewhere! F-f-find the treats ‹name›, take them b-b-back to Smokywood Pastures in Orgrimmar, and t-t-tell them I n-n-need to be unfrozen!","rew":"Experience: 3,300","back":"‹name› - our Feast of Winter Veil will be ruined without those treats to restock! Graccu himself will miss out on sharing his delicious meat pies with all the good boys and girls this season...","done":"You found it! You've saved Smokywood Pasture's Feast of Winter Veil!\nPoor Sacks... we'll be sure to send a team out there and figure out a way to unfreeze him. Hopefully, he'll be back in time for the day of the Feast; he'll need to make up missed time working though. Still, this wouldn't even be possible if it weren't for you!\nAlterac Mountains Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":35.4,"y":72.5,"n":"Strange Snowman","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":53.3,"y":66.5,"n":"Kaymard Copperpinch","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1463":{"id":1463,"t":"Earth Sapta","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Canaga Earthcaller for another Earth Sapta.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Sapta","done":"I give you one in good faith. You already proved yourself once, but me tinkin' you should be more careful in the future.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69.2,"n":"Canaga Earthcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"2983":{"id":2983,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Kranal Fiss in the Barrens.","desc":"It's been some time since you were tested last, ‹name›. You've been patient thus far in your studies, but it's time for you to learn about greater powers... it's time you learn real power. The element of fire is yours if you're prepared to pay for it.\nSeek out Kranal Fiss in the Barrens. He lives in a small dwelling north of the Crossroads, but be mindful, if you've reached the blasted night elf lands, you've gone way too far.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Hmmm, Swart sent you to me, did he?\nWell then, Swart could always be trusted, so that must mean you're ready to take part of the next sapta--the sapta of fire.\nI see it in your eyes already, the burning, the desire. You've tasted power, and now you're ready for more of it. Patience, ‹name›. Remember what earth taught you. Power and destruction will come easily, but you must still know when to stay your hand.\nDurotar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.4,"y":42.6,"n":"Swart","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":56,"y":19.9,"n":"Kranal Fiss","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94503":{"id":94503,"t":"Call of water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to the Minor Manifestation of Water in Westfall.","desc":"Light erupts as the final word leaves your lips. The hiss of water turning to mist fades into silence, and your senses reel as the corrupt spirits around you unravel, their essence scattered like ash in the wind.","done":"Thanks to you. Thanks to the shamans.\nCorruption ebbs but life continues to wane. Up to shamans to protect life.\nWestfall Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":45.6,"y":59.9,"n":"Forgotten Shrine","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":38.6,"y":44.6,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Water","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8743":{"id":8743,"t":"Bang a Gong!","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"The Scepter of the Shifting Sands","rew":"You will receive:\nBlack Qiraji Resonating Crystal\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"The Scarab Gong looms ominously before you. Steel yourself, ‹name›; for once the Scarab Gong is rung, the gates of Ahn'Qiraj will be opened.\nFrom the slackened maw of the beast can only come chaos and destruction. Defend your people!","done":"From the ground near the gong springs a special crystal. Perhaps favor from the Brood.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":25.7,"y":90.9,"n":"The Scarab Gong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8343":{"id":8343,"t":"Goldleaf's Discovery","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Aurel Goldleaf in Cenarion Hold.","desc":"‹name›, Aurel Goldleaf thinks she's found a way to summon and defeat a ruling member of the Abyssal Council! Such a task will be dangerous, but you have earned great respect amongst the Cenarion Circle. We know that if anyone can do it, you can.\nMay fortune go with you, ‹name›. Speak with Aurel when you are ready.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"What Huum says is true. I believe I know how to summon a lord of the Abyssal Council! Listen on, and I will explain...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.9,"n":"Huum Wildmane","s":1},{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"423":{"id":423,"t":"Arugal's Folly","lv":14,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles to Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\n6 Glutton Shackle Moonrage Glutton 80 %\n3 Darksoul Shackle Moonrage Darksoul 80 %","desc":"After examining Arugal's work my worst suspicions were confirmed. The old hack was not qualified to clean chamber pots in Dalaran let alone represent the Kirin Tor in its most dire hour. Fools!\nArugal used enchanted items to reinforce his weak magic. I need to examine these items first hand. Travel forth and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have collected enough of their enchanted shackles for my research. The foul creatures have been seen to the north and east.","rew":"Money: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I will need 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles before I can assess the situation and devise a final solution for Arugal. Now heed your bidding and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have what I need.","done":"I hope I can acquire enough energy from such a limited sample. Perhaps I should have had you get more shackles.\nNonetheless, you showed great skill in collecting these, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"1063":{"id":1063,"t":"The Elder Crone","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Magatha in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"To truly tend the spirits of Stonetalon we must consult the tauren elders.\nI do not know many of their leaders' names, but I do know of one: Magatha. I have heard that she is very old, and she knows much. If anyone can marshal spiritual aid from the tauren, it is she.\nMagatha resides in the tauren capital of Thunder Bluff, on Elder Rise -- the city's northeastern bluff. Speak with Magatha, and tell her of the peril of Stonetalon Mountains.","rew":"Experience: 675","done":"I bid you greetings. You are here seeking council?\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.3,"y":27.9,"n":"Seereth Stonebreak","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","e":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"343":{"id":343,"t":"Speaking of Fortitude","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Royal Library in Stormwind Keep and speak with Milton Sheaf. He can find for you the book on metallurgy that Brother Kristoff needs for his speech.","desc":"I'm giving a speech on the Fortitude of the Spirit, and I'd like to recite passages from a particular book on metallurgy - \"The Stresses of Iron.\" A copy of this book should be in the Royal Library, within Stormwind Keep. Can you retrieve it for me? If so, then may the blessings of the Light be with you!\nThe Royal Library is very large, but the head librarian, Milton Sheaf, knows each shelf like it was his own son. Speak to him, he'll retrieve the book for you.","rew":"Experience: 200\n+10 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Metallurgy? Ah yes, we have many books on the subject, and are happy to aid Brother Kristoff with his speech! Now...which particular book was it the good brother needed?","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":55,"y":54.2,"n":"Brother Kristoff","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":30.2,"n":"Milton Sheaf","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"6183":{"id":6183,"t":"Honor the Dead","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 660, 0.98 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Mathias Shaw again if you wish to accept his task.","desc":"Five of my best field agents were assigned the Marris case. One returned, only to end up dead in his sleep three days later.\nWhat little information we did manage to get out of him was incoherent gibberish. We made out two words: \"Nathanos\", and \"Blightcaller.\"\nI do not have the available manpower to continue this investigation and Ravenholdt will not assist us. We must get to the bottom of this; if only to provide closure to the families of the deceased. Will you help?","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"<Mathias nods.>\nI had faith that Bolvar would send me men and women of honor - the most dedicated soldiers of the Alliance.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"583":{"id":583,"t":"Welcome to the Jungle","lv":30,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Hemet Nesingwary","desc":"Welcome to Stranglethorn!\nPerhaps you're not aware of this, but that dwarf over there is the one and only Hemet Nesingwary, renowned war hero of the Alliance and master big game hunter. He's not one for welcoming strangers into his camp, but you look like you've seen quite a bit of action in your day, ‹class›.\nBeing a veteran of many battles himself, Master Nesingwary has a soft spot for fellow heroes.\nGo and speak with him. Perhaps he can give you some hunting pointers.","rew":"Experience: 250","done":"Jolly nice to make your acquaintance, ‹name›. Haven't seen a ‹class› around these parts for some time.\nI situated myself with this expedition for one purpose: to hunt a great and elusive beast. Seeing that you're a hero of sorts I am willing to let you take part in the hunt, but you must first prove yourself.\nI shall teach the ways of raptor killing to you. Ajeck will train you with tiger hunting. And Sir Erlgadin is a master of panther tracking.\nProve your skill and I'll let you in on the big hunt.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.8,"n":"Hemet Nesingwary","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8183":{"id":8183,"t":"The Heart of Hakkar","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 10,000, 1 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Heart of Hakkar to Molthor on Yojamba Isle.\nHeart of Hakkar Hakkar in Zul'Gurub\nProvided: Heart of Hakkar","desc":"The Heart of Hakkar burns from within. Although the Soulflayer is defeated, the kernel of his power yet remains in this cursed organ.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nZandalarian Hero Badge Zandalarian Hero Charm Zandalarian Hero Medallion\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"‹name›, the reek of an evil soul surrounds you. Have you been cursed by the Soulflayer?","done":"Ah, the Heart of Hakkar. So the Soulflayer has been slain! Our world is saved!\n‹name›, your service to us cannot be overstated. You truly are a hero of this realm!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15,"y":15.1,"n":"Molthor","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"5463":{"id":5463,"t":"Menethil's Gift","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Stratholme and find Menethil's Gift. Place the Keepsake of Remembrance upon the unholy ground.\nKeepsake of Remembrance Keepsake of Remembrance\nProvided: Keepsake of Remembrance","desc":"I watched as the human, Ras Frostwhisper, pledged his undying soul to the Lich King. He drew the dagger to his own throat and with a smile, cut from ear to ear. His body collapsed inside the borders of the pentagram. The Lich King stood over the fallen mage and with a single motion, Ras Frostwhisper the lich, was born.\n<Leonid gazes at the ground and then looks up at you.>\nYes, ‹race›, I remember. What you seek has a name - Menethil's Gift: The ground blessed by the Lich King - holy ground to Scourge.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The area around Menethil's Gift is exceptionally cold.","done":"You place the keepsake on the tainted soil.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","s":1}],"cats":["stratholme"]},"5863":{"id":5863,"t":"The Dunemaul Compound","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Andi Lynn in Gadgetzan wants you to destroy the Dunemaul Compound by killing 10 Dunemaul Brutes, 10 Dunemaul Enforcers, and Gor'marok the Ravager.\nDunemaul Brute slain : 0/ 10\nDunemaul Enforcer slain : 0/ 10\nGor'marok the Ravager slain","desc":"Just recently, a large band of nomadic ogres arrived in Tanaris. South of here, they have taken over a large area of the desert and formed a compound. Several smaller bands are currently wandering the desert, some of which have invaded the old troll ruins.\nThe Dunemaul Compound must be destroyed! We cannot allow these ogres to build up a force.\nThe leader of this band is named Gor'marok the Ravager; I believe that putting an end to his leadership will be the beginning of the end for the ogres.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWitherseed Gloves Rugwood Mantle\nExperience: 4,550\n+100 reputation with Gadgetzan","back":"I'm so worried! Please be careful!","done":"I'm so glad you were able to do this for me, ‹name›! Thanks for your help!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.8,"y":27.4,"n":"Andi Lynn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"7383":{"id":7383,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":11,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Amethyst Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nFilled Amethyst Phial\nProvided: Amethyst Phial","desc":"All was not well with Teldrassil, however. Staghelm's carefully made plans for the new World Tree had borne out as he had hoped, but there was one small problem, a problem to which many of the troubles on Teldrassil may be attributed.\nHowever, I will not get into that yet. You must visit the last moonwell, to the northwest in the Oracle Glade. Under the boughs of the Oracle Tree lies the first and most powerful of our wells. Retrieve a phial of its water and return to me.","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Along with the druids, the Oracle Tree and the Arch Druid have been carefully monitoring the growth of Teldrassil. But though we have a new home, our immortal lives have not been restored.","done":"To be in the presence of the Oracle Tree... it is almost to feel wisdom take form. Let me continue the telling...\nWith Teldrassil grown, the Arch Druid approached the dragons for their blessings, as the dragons had placed upon Nordrassil in ancient times. But Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused to give his blessing, chiding the druid for his arrogance. In agreement with Nozdormu, Alexstrasza also refused Staghelm, and without her blessing, Teldrassil's growth has been flawed and unpredictable...","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":61.7,"n":"Corithras Moonrage","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"903":{"id":903,"t":"Prowlers of the Barrens","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 7 Prowler Claws from Savannah Prowlers for Sergra Darkthorn in the Crossroads.\n7 Prowler Claws Savannah Prowler 80 %","desc":"Now it's time to go after something that really bites. The prowlers of the Barrens are a tough breed. Tough, resourceful, sly... and deadly. You'll find them among the tall grasses. You'll find many to the southwest of the Crossroads.\nBe wary as you hunt them, ‹name›, or you may find yourself no longer the predator, but instead the prey.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes your hunt, ‹name›? Have you found the prowlers?","done":"Ah, I see you've been busy, lurking in the grasses and hunting prowlers. Do you think, then, it is time to face a champion among them?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.2,"y":31,"n":"Sergra Darkthorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"4503":{"id":4503,"t":"Shizzle's Flyer","lv":51,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 8 Webbed Diemetradon Scales and 8 Webbed Pterrordax Scales for Shizzle in Marshal's Refuge.\n8 Webbed Diemetradon Scale Young Diemetradon 20 % , Diemetradon 20 % , Elder Diemetradon 20 %\n8 Webbed Pterrordax Scale Fledgling Pterrordax 20 % , Pterrordax 20 % , Frenzied Pterrordax 20 %","desc":"I'm making a flying machine!\nI got stranded here, and I'm absolutely horrible at finding my way around. I'd take a gryphon or wind rider back to Gadgetzan, but those beasts just scare me to death.\nSo, will you help me? All I have left to build is the wings, and I was thinking that the webby scales from the pterrordax and diemetradon would be perfect. There's no way I'm going to go up against one of those, but you look pretty tough. Why don't you give it a try?","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nShizzle's Drizzle Blocker Shizzle's Muzzle Shizzle's Nozzle Wiper\nExperience: 4,900","back":"Every great vehicle needs a name... I was thinking I'd call it... Pwned!","done":"Yes, these scales are perfect. I should be able to get this flyer off the ground with these scales for sure!\nThanks!","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.2,"y":11.6,"n":"Shizzle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"7623":{"id":7623,"t":"Lord Banehollow","lv":58,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Purchase Shadowy Potions from Gorzeeki in the Burning Steppes.\nUse the potions to travel through Jaedenar, and speak with Lord Banehollow.","desc":"Mor'zul says that you want to open a portal to Xoroth. To do that, you'll need Xorothian stardust. That's not easy to find on Azeroth!\nThere is one being who might have some: Lord Banehollow in Jaedenar, the seat of the Shadow Council! Speak with him and he might part with the stardust.\nBut if you're going to Jaedenar, then you'll need to cloak yourself in the Shadow Council's own flavor of evil. That will require some of my shadowy potions, and that will cost you...","rew":"Experience: 6,200","done":"My patience spans the millenia, warlock. But do not think that allows you more than an instant of my time...\nBurning Steppes Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":12.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Gorzeeki Wildeyes","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":35.9,"y":44.4,"n":"Lord Banehollow","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1703":{"id":1703,"t":"Mathiel","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Furen's Notes to Mathiel.\nFuren's Notes\nProvided: Furen's Notes","desc":"I made a copy of my notes on the techniques I learned while making your armor, and need them sent to the blacksmith Mathiel. He lives in Darnassus which is quite a long way off, but I'm sure he'll be very grateful to learn what I've learned.","rew":"Experience: 1,150","back":"I bid you greetings, ‹class›.","done":"I bid you greetings, warrior.\nStormwind City Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":59.5,"y":45.4,"n":"Mathiel","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8423":{"id":8423,"t":"Warrior Kinship","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 7 Helboar in the Blasted Lands and return to the Fallen Hero of the Horde.\nHelboar slain : 0/ 7","desc":"<The Hero looks you over.>\nYou are a ‹class›, no doubt. I would ask an honorable task of you, but I must test your strength.\nIt is said that Rexxar would measure the sharpness of his blades by killing a helboar with a single, swift strike. Now I will measure your strength by killing them.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"The burning spines of the helboar leave horrific scars. Do not fear the pain and disfigurement, warrior, they are nothing compared to the prison to which I am bound.","done":"I need no proof to know what you have done, warrior. I can see the determination etched in your expression.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":34.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Fallen Hero of the Horde","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5223":{"id":5223,"t":"Return to Chillwind Camp","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,800 experience instead of 5,800, 0.48 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp, Western Plaguelands.\nFilled Writhing Haunt Bottle\nProvided: Filled Writhing Haunt Bottle","desc":"You delicately top off the empty bottle; a sample of the foul substance that churns under the platform of the cauldron now oozes back and forth inside the fragile glass container.\nWith the poison in hand, it is time to return to High Priestess MacDonnell at Chillwind Camp to complete the mission.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,800\n+50 reputation with Stormwind\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Once we successfully analyze the sample drawn from the Writhing Haunt's cauldron, it will provide us with a third avenue to deliver a devastating counter agent onto the Scourge!","done":"Another finely executed mission, ‹name›! This makes three cauldrons available to us to turn against the Scourge. If Kel'Thuzad's necromantic dominance over these lands wasn't as strong as it currently is, I'd dare say you'd shut them down completely!\nAlchemist Arbington will have a report on what this cauldron - as well as the other cauldrons subverted - will require to deliver our counter agent to the plague. With that, the time has come to bring the last cauldron of the west under our influence!","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53,"y":65.6,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"6023":{"id":6023,"t":"Unfinished Business","lv":57,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Huntsman Radley and Cavalier Durgen before returning to Kirsta Deepshadow in Western Plaguelands.\nHuntsman Radley slain\nCavalier Durgen slain","desc":"My real mission was to weaken the Scarlet Crusade's outlying forces and then infiltrate Hearthglen to gauge their numbers. I'm still in no shape to do it on my own, so perhaps I could ask you to aid me again, ‹name›? From what information I gathered before being discovered, the Crusade has two important members that are the backbone of their forces outside the town: Huntsman Radley and Cavalier Durgen. Kill them, and we're making progress. They should be along Hearthglen Pass outside the town proper.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,000","back":"Have you found them yet, ‹name›? With the two of them taken care of, I can proceed to enter Hearthglen to take a closer look at their setup. I can't do it without your help. Please, find Radley and Durgen for me.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You've been more help than I could have hoped for. The air here just seems to suck my will. I feel tired, and I can tell I'm not getting any better the longer I'm here.\nI'm not really sure how I'm going to infiltrate Hearthglen itself and report on how strong the Scarlet Crusade's presence is.\nBut that's another matter, before you leave, here, take this... as payment for your help. Thank you again.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":51.9,"y":28.1,"n":"Kirsta Deepshadow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"103":{"id":103,"t":"Keeper of the Flame","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Flasks of Oil to Captain Grayson at the Westfall Lighthouse.\n5 Flask of Oil Harvest Reaper 38.2 % , Harvest Watcher 34.8 % , Harvest Golem 34.6 % , Rusty Harvest Golem 34.3 % and 4 more","desc":"The night the Lighthouse Keeper's family died was horrible. I watched, helpless, as Old Murk-Eye led the attack. But what's done is done and now my concern is for the lives of the sailors on The Great Sea whose ships come close to the perilous rocks of the coastline. With no one to keep watch on the flame the responsibility has fallen upon me.\nHelp me keep the torch lit by bringing me 5 flasks of oil from the Harvest Monsters.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n3 Minor Mana Potion 3 Minor Healing Potion\nYou will also receive:\nScroll of Intellect Scroll of Stamina\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150","back":"The flame will not burn for long without oil, ‹name›.","done":"Praise you, brave ‹class›. The rocks of the Westfall Coast shall be lit thanks to your hard work. Many lives will be spared so long as the torch is kept lit.\nI died needlessly on this very shore. My afterlife plight is to see that no others follow my destiny.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":30,"y":86,"n":"Captain Grayson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"3783":{"id":3783,"t":"Are We There, Yeti?","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 10 Thick Yeti Furs for Umi Rumplesnicker in Everlook.\n10 Thick Yeti Fur Ice Thistle Yeti 33 % , Rogue Ice Thistle 33 %","desc":"My friends are always coming up with great ideas. I've never felt like I could match them... until today! I just drew up the plans for something great! If you promise not to tell, I'll let you in on the secret...\nI'm going to make a mechanical yeti! Not only are my friends sure to be freaked out when they see it, but when they get over that, I know they'll be impressed!\nI need thick yeti fur from the ice thistle yeti to start with. Will you help? You'll find them to the southeast.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,350\n+75 reputation with Everlook","back":"I've got lots to get started on here. Please get me those furs as soon as you can!","done":"These furs are perfect, ‹name›. We're off to a great start here!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":60.9,"y":37.6,"n":"Umi Rumplesnicker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"5063":{"id":5063,"t":"Cap of the Scarlet Savant","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays -50g instead of 0.","obj":"In order to create the Cap of the Scarlet Savant, you will be required to bring the following items back to Malyfous Darkhammer: 1 Pristine Hide of the Beast; 5 Frayed Abomination Stitchings; 8 Arcane Crystals; 5 Enchanted Scarlet Thread.\nYou will also be required to pay 50 gold pieces for the crafting of the item.\nItem #12731\n5 Frayed Abomination Stitching\n8 Arcane Crystal\n5 Enchanted Scarlet Thread\nRequired money: 50","desc":"A finer cap you may never see. From the pristine hide of the beast, our expert crafters will create the most phenomenal hat a prestidigitator could ever hope to don!\nFifty gold pieces along with the listed items and your head shall be graced with the Cap of the Scarlet Savant:\n*The pristine hide of the Beast.\n*Frayed abomination stitchings.\n*Arcane crystals.\n*Enchanted scarlet thread.\nBEHOLD!","rew":"You will receive:\nCap of the Scarlet Savant","back":"Unless you've got everything I need, you're wasting my time.","done":"Astounding! It must have taken weeks to gather those components... and how did you find a pristine hide?!?\nEnjoy the cap, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous's Catalogue","s":1},{"z":"Winterspring","x":61,"y":38.8,"n":"Malyfous Darkhammer","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"8103":{"id":8103,"t":"The Pebble of Kajaro","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Pebble of Kajaro","rew":"You will receive:\nPebble of Kajaro\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Hakkari fear you, ‹name›. They speak of horrors they believed that only their faceless God could perpetrate. You have burned them with the force of Kajaro. They now know fear in two places.\nIt is time to further strengthen the pebble. Hand me the talisman.","done":"Continue in your decimation of the trolls of Zul'Gurub. Hakkar must see that the world will not buckle beneath his indomitable will.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});